# CHANGELOG

This is the durable running repo changelog going forward.

Historical one-off reports such as `STEP6_CHANGELOG_REPORT.txt` remain useful background, but new repo changes should be logged here.

## 2026-04-21
- Added a bounded validation-only Step 6.7B controller override for the `2026-04-19_012531` fallback audit after the clean GPU rerun showed that the model path can run but still only rescues 1 of the 13 unresolved cases while 20 semantically weak deterministic rescues are skipped before the model ever sees them. Updated `src/kc_l/kc_drafting/seed_floor_triage.py` so validation config can set `model_rescue.validation_force_model_for_all_rescue_eligible: true`, which keeps deterministic rescue as a logged probe but prevents it from short-circuiting rescue-eligible seed-floor fallbacks before bounded model rescue. The new path preserves default behavior when the flag is absent, records the validation flag in `seed_floor_triage`, and is intended only to answer the validation question of whether the model can outperform the weak deterministic rescues on all 33 rescue-eligible fallbacks.

## 2026-04-20
- Hardened Step 6.7B model-rescue execution against malformed or empty Ollama JSON outputs without changing retrieval or rescue semantics. Replaced `src/kc_l/utils/ollama_json.py` with a more resilient parser that can strip fenced blocks, remove `<think>...</think>` sections, extract the first balanced JSON object from mixed text, and raise explicit empty-content / parse-failure errors with raw previews instead of raw `JSONDecodeError`s. In `src/kc_l/kc_drafting/seed_floor_triage.py`, made `_call_model_rescue(...)` honor `Step67ModelRuntime.max_retries` and converted unrecoverable model-rescue exceptions into bounded per-KC outcomes (`error_empty_content`, `error_json_parse`, `error_timeout`, or class-based fallback errors) so a single bad model response no longer aborts the entire Step 6.7B run. This patch was motivated by the real Sofja validation failure from job `201778`, where the corrected Slurm job reached live model inference and then died on JSON parsing in the 6.7B rescue path.

## 2026-04-19

- Introduced the first persistent Step 6.75 evidence-grounded draft canonicalization stage without changing Step 6.7, Step 6.8, Step 5.3, or Step 6.6 behavior. Added `src/kc_l/kc_drafting/canonicalization.py` plus the new orchestration entrypoint `run_step6_75_pipeline(...)` in `src/kc_l/kc_drafting/orchestration.py`, the new runner `steps/step_06_75_kc_draft_canonicalization/scripts/run_step6_75_kc_draft_canonicalization.py`, and the default resource config `steps/step_06_75_kc_draft_canonicalization/resources/step6_75.slice10.yaml`. The new stage preserves raw Step 6.7 bundle fields untouched, emits parallel `definition_full_candidate_canonicalized` and `scope_candidate_canonicalized` fields, and adds auditable canonicalization metadata including mode, actions, evidence ids, residual uncertainty flags, and review-burden estimates. First-pass canonicalization is strictly deterministic and extractive: whitespace/punctuation cleanup, scaffold/tail trimming, and same-evidence quote-surface preference for definition fields only. Expanded `tests/test_kc_drafting_architecture.py` with focused Step 6.75 regressions for identity/no-op, deterministic cleanup, same-support quote selection, unsafe raw passthrough, persistent JSONL/stat emission, and runner delegation. Local validation passed with `python -m py_compile ...`, direct invocation of 6 focused checks, and real `2026-04-19_012531` artifact replay proving one identity case (`KC_CLU_DBS_003`), one cleanup case (`KC_EVAL_BASIC_005`), one same-evidence extractive selection case (`KC_CLU_HIER_004`), and one explicit raw-passthrough case (`KC_CLF_NB_004`); `python -m pytest ...` still fails in this mirror because `pytest` is not installed, and no Step 6.75 full replay or authoritative rerun was performed.
- Narrowed the generic Step 6.7 `definition_full_candidate_draft_supported_single_span_fallback` direct-admission seam in `src/kc_l/utils/kc_step67_model_drafting.py` after the tiny synced `2026-04-19_103119` diagnostics proved the previous legitimacy tightening had overblocked direct admission down to `20 / 80 / 44` while still keeping zero baseline regressions. Added `_fallback_surface_history_or_provenance_like(...)` and `_fallback_surface_name_led_direct_quality(...)`, then refined `_fallback_surface_strong_enough_for_direct(...)` so generic fallback quotes can now recover as `direct_grounded` when they are strongly target-aligned standalone definitions with either an explicit definition cue or a narrow name-led direct-quality predicate, while history/provenance exact-name sentences are demoted instead of surviving as direct. Expanded `tests/test_kc_drafting_architecture.py` with focused regressions for explicit-definition-relation direct recovery, history/provenance demotion, and narrow name-led standalone direct recovery. Local validation passed with `python -m py_compile ...`, direct invocation of 10 focused tests, and artifact-driven replay over the real `2026-04-19_012531` bundles showing the generic fallback-direct helper shifts from the prior `5 / 46 / 11` replay shape to `7 / 46 / 9`, newly recovers `KC_CLU_HIER_004`, `KC_CLU_HIER_005`, and `KC_FSEL_FW_001` as direct, keeps `KC_CLU_EVAL_002` direct, demotes the bad `KC_CLU_KM_001` history sentence to normalized, and still keeps the previously audited bad-direct family out of `direct_grounded`; `python -m pytest ...` still fails in this mirror because `pytest` is not installed, and no new Step 6.7 rerun was performed.
- Tightened the generic Step 6.7 `definition_full_candidate_draft_supported_single_span_fallback` direct-admission seam in `src/kc_l/utils/kc_step67_model_drafting.py` without touching Step 5.3, Step 6.6, or Step 6.8. Added `_surface_starts_with_name_variant(...)`, `_fallback_surface_strong_enough_for_direct(...)`, and `_fallback_surface_safe_for_normalized_candidate(...)`, then rewired `_definition_draft_supported_single_span_fallback_value(...)` so late control-fallback directs must now satisfy stronger standalone-definition legitimacy and target-alignment checks, while thin but source-faithful fallback surfaces can still normalize instead of staying direct. Preserved the same-KC salvage framework, preserved the name-led equation identity exception needed for `KC_CLU_EVAL_002`, and expanded `tests/test_kc_drafting_architecture.py` with focused regressions for weak-target blocking, equation-identity preservation, and name-led contextual demotion. Local validation passed with `python -m py_compile ...`, direct invocation of 12 focused fallback/salvage tests, and artifact-driven replay against real `2026-04-19_012531` bundles showing all 10 explicitly-audited bad direct examples now move out of `direct_grounded` at helper level (`1` abstain, `9` normalized), the full `62` generic fallback-direct cases replay to `{direct: 5, normalized: 46, abstain: 11}`, and the accepted-baseline direct guard still preserves `KC_CLU_EVAL_002` as direct; `python -m pytest ...` still fails in this mirror because `pytest` is not installed, and no new Step 6.7 rerun was performed.
- Narrowed the Step 6.7 same-KC salvage direct-admission seam in `src/kc_l/utils/kc_step67_model_drafting.py` so a same-KC local salvage row can return to `direct_grounded` only when it becomes a complete standalone definition via a tiny source-faithful tail trim, instead of being over-demoted to normalized. Added `_trim_salvage_surface_tail_fragment(...)`, wired a salvage-only `tail_trimmed` path into `_salvage_surface_strong_enough_for_direct(...)`, and kept the earlier legitimacy tightening intact for the noisy salvage pool. Expanded `tests/test_kc_drafting_architecture.py` with a helper regression and a bundle-level regression for the `i.e.,` tail-trim case. Local validation passed with `python -m py_compile ...`, direct invocation of 9 targeted salvage tests plus 15 broader fallback/salvage tests, and artifact-driven replay over the real `2026-04-18_234130` regression showing `KC_EVAL_BASIC_005` now upgrades from normalized to direct via `KC_EVAL_BASIC_005:overlay:d78d3049de73c3fb`, while the compact replay over the previously noisy `191023 -> 211250` recovered-direct set stays at `{direct: 2, normalized: 0, abstain: 8}`; `python -m pytest ...` still fails in this mirror because `pytest` is not installed, and no new Step 6.7 rerun was performed.
- Tightened the bounded Step 6.7 same-KC local salvage admission rule in `src/kc_l/utils/kc_step67_model_drafting.py` without touching Step 6.8, Step 5.3, or Step 6.6. Added salvage-specific named-alignment checks, narrowed salvage direct admission to genuinely standalone definition-quality same-KC local rows, kept a narrow salvage-specific override for definition-like broad-expository rows, and tightened salvage normalization so weakly aligned formula/procedure/context rows now abstain instead of being normalized through the salvage seam. Expanded `tests/test_kc_drafting_architecture.py` with focused regressions for broad-expository-but-definitional salvage direct admission and blocking of weakly aligned formula salvage. Local validation passed with `python -m py_compile ...`, direct invocation of 13 focused fallback/salvage tests, and artifact-driven replay over the real `2026-04-18_211250` recovered-direct seam showing the tightened helper now yields `{direct: 1, normalized: 1, abstain: 8}` by preserving `KC_CLU_HIER_006` as direct, demoting `KC_EVAL_BASIC_005` to normalized, and blocking the remaining eight noisy recovered directs; `python -m pytest ...` still fails in this mirror because `pytest` is not installed, and no new Step 6.7 rerun was performed.

